      "settings": {
        "custom_liquid": "{%- comment -%}\n  This code checks if any policies have been created in the Shopify Admin.\n  If policies exist, it creates an unordered list (<ul>) and then\n  loops through each policy object.\n\n  For each policy, it creates a list item (<li>) with a link (<a>).\n  The link's destination (href) is the policy's URL (policy.url),\n  and the link's text is the policy's title (policy.title).\n{%- endcomment -%}\n\n<style>.policy-list-container {\n  display: flex;\n  flex-direction: column;   /* This stacks the items vertically in a column. */\n  justify-content: center;  /* This centers the content vertically. */\n  align-items: center;      /* This centers the content horizontally. */\n  min-height: 80vh;         /* Ensures the container takes up most of the screen's height. */\n  text-align: center;       /* Centers the text within each list item. */\n}\n\n/* This targets the <ul> list itself. */\n.policy-list-container ul {\n  padding: 0;               /* Removes the default list padding. */\n  list-style-type: none;    /* Hides the default bullet points. */\n}\n\n/* This adds some space between each policy link. */\n.policy-list-container li {\n  margin: 15px 0; /* Adds 15px of space above and below each item. */\n}\n\n/* Basic styling for the links. */\n.policy-list-container a {\n  color: #121212;            /* Sets a dark color for the link text. */\n  text-decoration: none;      /* Removes the default underline. */\n  font-size: 1.1em;           /* Makes the font slightly larger. */\n  transition: color 0.2s ease; /* Adds a smooth color change on hover. */\n}\n\n/* A simple hover effect to show the link is interactive. */\n.policy-list-container a:hover {\n  color: #595959;             /* Changes the text color to a medium gray on hover. */\n  text-decoration: underline; /* Adds an underline on hover. */\n}</style>\n<div class=\"policy-list-container\">\n  {%- comment -%}\n    This code checks if any policies have been created in the Shopify Admin.\n    If policies exist, it creates an unordered list (<ul>) and then\n    loops through each policy object.\n  {%- endcomment -%}\n\n  {% if shop.policies %}\n    <ul>\n      {% for policy in shop.policies %}\n        <li>\n          <a href=\"{{ policy.url }}\">{{ policy.title }}</a>\n        </li>\n      {% endfor %}\n    </ul>\n  {% endif %}\n</div>",
